"If it takes 3kangaroos traveling at the same speed a total of 18 hours to travel across a highway, how many hours will it take four turtles, each traveling at half the speed of a kangaroo, to do so?","If it takes 3 kangaroos traveling at the same speed a total of 18 hours to travel across a highway, how many hours will it take four turtles, each traveling at half the speed of a kangaroo, to do so?",48,48,27,36,"- Let one kangaroo’s rate be r (job per hour). Then 3 kangaroos have rate 3r and finish in 18 hours, so 3r × 18 = 1 job ⇒ r = 1/54 job/hour.
- Each turtle moves at half a kangaroo’s speed, so each turtle’s rate is r/2. Four turtles have combined rate 4 × (r/2) = 2r.
- Time for four turtles = 1 ÷ (2r) = 1 ÷ (2 × 1/54) = 27 hours.

