- Each turtle moves at half a kangaroo’s speed, so each turtle’s rate is r/2. Four turtles have combined rate 4 × (r/2) = 2r.
- Time for four turtles = 1 ÷ (2r) = 1 ÷ (2 × 1/54) = 27 hours.
#### 27","Step 1: The time to cross a fixed distance depends on speed, not on how many animals are traveling. So if 3 kangaroos (each at the same speed) take 18 hours to cross, that means one kangaroo at that speed takes 18 hours.

